## Method, and why it is this method

`platforms/x960.md` §7F.2 records this platform reading `Enabled` while the service is actually
refused, and §7F.10 records `no service ssh ip` **replacing** the running-config line with
`service ssh ipv6` rather than writing a negation -- so **a config grep for `no service ssh ip`
finds nothing on a unit whose IPv4 SSH is off**. Neither `show ssh server` nor a config grep can
therefore carry this verdict. It is graded on **IPv4 TCP/22 on the wire**.

Instrument: **`tools/arpleg.py --tcp`**, the leg tool group B extended for T33386 the same day.
It sends a crafted SYN and reports the reply flags, where `SA` = the port is open, `R`/`RA` =
the service refused it, and **no reply row at all** = the frame was dropped. Every leg also
carries an **ICMP control to the same address**, so "the DUT refused TCP/22" is always told
apart from "the DUT was not there". No credential is ever offered, so no leg can cost a failed
login -- which matters on a bench where two accounts are already locked.

A **port 23 control** rides in every leg: telnet is off on this DUT (`no service telnet`), so
`:23` must answer `RA` in all four legs. It is the instrument's own witness that an `RA` is
being decoded correctly.

```
sudo arpleg.py --tag <tag> --out /tmp/ntp1021/T33380 --iface eth3 \
     --tcp 10.38.22.34:22,10.38.22.34:23 --icmp 10.38.22.34 \
     --sender-ip 10.38.22.33 --sender-mac 00:0d:b9:55:77:0e \
     --gw-mac e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43 --count 4 --wait 4
```

## The limb, in four legs

### LEG A -- baseline, SSH on both families (tag `t380-base`)

```
  cap t380-base-eth3.pcap: 30 frame(s)
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.33:40000 -> 10.38.22.34:22   S   [ours]
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.34:22    -> 10.38.22.33:40000 SA
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.33:40000 -> 10.38.22.34:22   R
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.33:40000 -> 10.38.22.34:23   S   [ours]
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.34:23    -> 10.38.22.33:40000 RA
    x4   ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.33 -> 10.38.22.34      [ours]
    x4   ICMP t0/c0 10.38.22.34 -> 10.38.22.33      [ours]
    x1   ARP-REQ who-has 10.38.22.34 tell 10.38.22.33
    x1   ARP-REPLY 10.38.22.34 is-at e0:1a:ea:d4:70:43
```
**4 of 4 SYNs to :22 answered `SA`** -- IPv4 SSH is open. `:23` answers `RA` and ICMP is 4/4.
This output is frame-for-frame identical to T33386's own `base-eth3` leg earlier the same day,
which is the instrument's cross-run control.

### LEG B -- `no service ssh ip` applied (tag `t380-v6only`)

```
awplus(config)#no service ssh ip
awplus#show running-config | include service ssh
service ssh ipv6                       <- the line was REPLACED, not negated (§7F.10)
awplus#show ssh server
SSH Server : Enabled                   <- still "Enabled" (§7F.2)
Protocol   : IPv6
```
```
  cap t380-v6only-eth3.pcap: 24 frame(s)
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.33:40000 -> 10.38.22.34:22   S   [ours]
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.34:22    -> 10.38.22.33:40000 RA        <- REFUSED
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.33:40000 -> 10.38.22.34:23   S   [ours]
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.34:23    -> 10.38.22.33:40000 RA
    x4   ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.33 -> 10.38.22.34      [ours]
    x4   ICMP t0/c0 10.38.22.34 -> 10.38.22.33      [ours]
```
`:22` flipped from `SA` to `RA` while **ICMP stayed 4 of 4** -- the host is up and reachable and
the service is refusing. That is the discrimination the whole limb rests on.

### LEG C -- the limb itself: after a cold boot, nothing typed

```
awplus#write
Building configuration...
[OK]
awplus#show startup-config | include service ssh
service ssh ipv6                       <- saved

tools/tb ckreload tb277 ntp1021 u2 115200 240
17:37:54 >>> reload   (04:37:54 UTC)
reboot question: 'reboot system? (y/n):' -> y
17:38:54 login seen after 60 s
```

🔬 **The first post-boot leg was DISCARDED, not graded.** Run 9 s after the login prompt it
returned:
```
  cap t380-afterboot-eth3.pcap: 16 frame(s)
    x4   TCP  ...:22  S [ours]      (no reply row at all)
    x4   TCP  ...:23  S [ours]      (no reply row at all)
    x4   ICMP t8/c0 ... [ours]
    x1   ICMP t0/c0 10.38.22.34 -> 10.38.22.33     <- only 1 of 4 answered
    x1   ARP-REQ who-has 10.38.22.33 tell 10.38.22.34
```
**The ICMP control answered 1 of 4 and the DUT was still ARPing for the box**, so the unit had
not finished coming up. With this tool "no reply row at all" means *silently dropped*, which is
precisely the wrong conclusion to draw here -- it would have read as a filter. The leg was
thrown away, the leg settled (`ping -c 4` -> **4/4, 0% loss, avg 0.442 ms**), and the
measurement re-taken. This is the same post-reload transient group C recorded as a spurious
`CHECK_CABLE`: **ping first, then measure.**

The real leg, 41 s after the login prompt, with **nothing typed into the DUT** (tag
`t380-afterboot2`):
```
  cap t380-afterboot2-eth3.pcap: 24 frame(s)
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.33:40000 -> 10.38.22.34:22   S   [ours]
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.34:22    -> 10.38.22.33:40000 RA        <- STILL REFUSED
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.33:40000 -> 10.38.22.34:23   S   [ours]
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.34:23    -> 10.38.22.33:40000 RA
    x4   ICMP t8/c0 10.38.22.33 -> 10.38.22.34      [ours]
    x4   ICMP t0/c0 10.38.22.34 -> 10.38.22.33      [ours]
```
**ICMP 4 of 4, TCP/22 refused 4 of 4** -- byte-identical to leg B, taken across a cold boot with
no configuration typed. Only then was the console opened to read the configuration:
```
awplus#show running-config | include service ssh
service ssh ipv6
awplus#show ssh server
SSH Server : Enabled
Protocol   : IPv6
```

**The restriction survived the reboot, and it was proven on the wire BEFORE it was read from a
`show`** -- which is the right order for a platform whose `show ssh server` says `Enabled` for a
service that is refusing connections.

### LEG D -- restore, and the arc closes (tag `t380-restored`)

```
awplus(config)#service ssh ip
awplus#show running-config | include service ssh
service ssh                            <- the suffix is dropped again
awplus#show ssh server
Protocol   : IPv4,IPv6
```
```
  cap t380-restored-eth3.pcap: 30 frame(s)
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.34:22 -> 10.38.22.33:40000 SA           <- open again
    x4   TCP  10.38.22.34:23 -> 10.38.22.33:40000 RA
    x4   ICMP t0/c0 10.38.22.34 -> 10.38.22.33    [ours]
```

**The full arc on the wire: `SA` -> `RA` -> (cold boot) `RA` -> `SA`.** Four legs, 16 SYNs to
:22, 16 to :23 and 16 ICMP echoes, with the port-23 control answering `RA` in all four.

