## What run 2 adds

1. 🔴 **`no service ssh ip` IS persistent across a reload, and it is persistent on the wire.**
   Saved as `service ssh ipv6`, it came back after a 60 s cold boot with IPv4 TCP/22 refusing
   4 of 4 SYNs while ICMP answered 4 of 4, with nothing typed into the device. **T33380's
   reboot-persistence limb is no longer NOT MEASURED.**
2. 🔬 **A post-reload leg needs the link proved before it is read.** A leg run 9 s after the
   login prompt showed *no TCP reply rows at all* and 1 of 4 ICMP -- and with `arpleg --tcp`,
   "no reply row" means *silently dropped*, i.e. it would have read as a filter rather than as a
   unit still booting. Ping to 4/4 first, then measure. The same transient that produced group
   C's spurious `CHECK_CABLE`.
3. **A fifth independent measurement of the 60 s cold boot** on this platform
   (60, 60, 60, 61, 60 s across this campaign).

